error[E0277]: `Vec<&str>` is not an argument of type `Vec<String>`
  --> tests/compile_fail_client/arg_vec_of_str.rs:12:18
   |
12 |     api.issues().list(vec!["C-bug"]).await
   |                  ^^^^ not an argument of type `Vec<String>`
   |
   = help: the trait `Arg<Vec<String>>` is not implemented for `Vec<&str>`
   = note: an argument of type `Vec<String>` takes that type, or a reference to it when it is `Clone`, which is cloned; a `String` takes a `&str` too, and a `Vec` an array or a slice of what an item takes
   = note: no number becomes another: convert it first, with `From`, or `try_into()?` where it may not fit; an `Option<String>` takes `Some("x".into())`, and a `Vec<String>` `["a"]` rather than `vec!["a"]`
   = help: the following other types implement trait `Arg<T>`:
             `&&str` implements `Arg<String>`
             `&T` implements `Arg<T>`
             `&[A; N]` implements `Arg<Vec<T>>`
             `&[A]` implements `Arg<Vec<T>>`
             `&str` implements `Arg<String>`
             `[A; N]` implements `Arg<Vec<T>>`
note: required by a bound in `Issues::list::{anon_assoc#0}`
  --> tests/compile_fail_client/arg_vec_of_str.rs:6:55
